<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benjamin of Tudela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1173</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benjamin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudela">Tudela</a> was a Jewish traveller from Tudela in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> who journeyed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> through southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, probably between about 1165 and 1173. His Book of Travels, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>, describes the Jewish communities he found and gives valuable information on the cities, trade and rulers of the twelfth-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benjamin-of-tudela.jpg" alt="Benjamin of Tudela" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jialxv · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benjam%C3%ADn_de_Tudela_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
